  "version": 4,
  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "2026-10-06: every number the individual return uses for AY 2026-27 (FY 2025-26), both regimes - slabs by age, 87A, surcharge, cess, the 111A/112A rates and 1.25 lakh exemption, standard deduction, family pension, house property, Chapter VI-A caps, HRA percentages and the ITR-1 limits. A new year = a new row of numbers here, nothing else. 2026-10-06: via_status - an HUF claims 80C, 80D (for a member), 80G and 80TTA; 80CCC / 80CCD, 80E, 80U and 80TTB are for individuals. 2026-10-06: 80DD, 80DDB, 80EE, 80EEA, 80EEB, 80GG, 80GGC - old regime only; an HUF claims 80DD, 80DDB and 80GGC too. 2026-10-07: rate_115bb / rate_115bbj / rate_115bbh (30%, both regimes, no basic exemption, no 87A, no Chapter VI-A against them) and agri_integrate_above 5,000 (partial integration, both regimes).",
